WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:08.340
Callbacks, drag queens, and Star Trek. What else&nbsp;
could you expect from the Hocus Pocus sequel? Here&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:12.900
are some of the best blink-and-you'll-miss-it&nbsp;
moments, and beware: spoilers ahead!

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:20.040
The Salem of Hocus Pocus 2 is a town just as&nbsp;
obsessed with witchcraft and Halloween as it was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:25.200
in the original film. However, this time, viewers&nbsp;
are also treated to the Salem Halloween festival,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:30.840
featuring the 'famous' Sandy's Candy&nbsp;
Cauldron and an apple-bobbing booth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:35.940
that doubles as a drowning pool. Salem,&nbsp;
in fact, is so obsessed with its heritage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:40.200
that it leans into its witch-burning&nbsp;
history a little too hard sometimes.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:45.660
As Becca and Izzy head for the Magic Shop&nbsp;
after school, Mayor Traske stops them to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:50.880
wish Becca a happy birthday. As they chat, a&nbsp;
woman dressed as a witch can be seen behind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:55.500
them. The odd thing about the scene? She's&nbsp;
tied to a tree with a pyre built under her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.500 --> 00:01:00.960
posing for photos while a man dressed as a Puritan&nbsp;
holds the camera. It's a small moment barely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:05.760
visible in the background and easy to miss, but&nbsp;
subtly adds to the world-building all the same.

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:12.420
Hocus Pocus 2 weaves Salem's history in with the&nbsp;
modern day, creating a running gag throughout&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:17.340
the whole length of the film. Audiences might&nbsp;
have noticed the film's large number of Puritan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:22.140
references, recalling the movie's opening shots&nbsp;
when Reverend Traske banishes young Winnifred.

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:27.060
In the present day, the high school mascot&nbsp;
is a Puritan, clearly visible through all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:31.740
the scenes set in the school, as well as on&nbsp;
Mike and his fellow football players' jerseys.

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:35.160
Later, the Sanderson sisters&nbsp;
stumble on a look-alike contest,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:38.460
decided by a group of judges dressed as Puritans.

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:44.820
"If these are all worshippers…"
"...then this must be the altar."

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:48.480
It's clearly an element of the&nbsp;
town's history that holds a lot of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:52.920
meaning – even if you have to give the movie&nbsp;
a second watch to spot all the references.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:58.560
The Hocus Pocus costume department has&nbsp;
always been part of the film's charm,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:03.300
especially since building an entire&nbsp;
town full of Halloween fans requires&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:08.100
a lot of creativity. The original Hocus&nbsp;
Pocus film used authentic costumes from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:12.840
other Disney movies. Naturally, the&nbsp;
Hocus Pocus 2 costume department also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:17.640
gave audiences the chance to find several&nbsp;
cheeky call-backs to the original film.

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:20.430
"Mom?"
"Hm?"&nbsp;

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:24.540
"What are you supposed to be?"
"Madonna."

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:29.280
In Hocus Pocus 2, look for the return of Madonna&nbsp;
stomping away in the street during the musical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:34.440
dance number. Fans might also have seen that&nbsp;
the Supremes are back. In the original film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:38.340
the trio of women wearing sparkly red&nbsp;
dresses can be seen in the front row,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:44.340
right below the stage, becoming bewitched along&nbsp;
with the rest of the crowd. In Hocus Pocus 2,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.340 --> 00:02:48.480
all three are dancing through&nbsp;
town in the spellbound flash mob.

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:55.260
One of the classic scenes in the original&nbsp;
Hocus Pocus is when the Sanderson sisters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.260 --> 00:03:00.720
encounter the flirtatious devil, his&nbsp;
disappointed wife, and their demonic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:07.020
yappy little dog. Back in 1993, the devil was&nbsp;
played by the legendary Garry Marshall in an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:12.120
uncredited cameo. His wife was played by his&nbsp;
real-life sister and actress, Penny Marshall.

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:18.120
Though both stars are sadly deceased, the&nbsp;
two lovable oddball characters are back in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:24.600
Hocus Pocus 2 for those who watch closely. While&nbsp;
searching for Mayor Traske, Winnifred flies past&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:30.600
the window of a house where two men are watching&nbsp;
that scene on TV. Later, we see two people dressed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:36.180
in costume as the devil and his wife standing&nbsp;
behind Mayor Traske in line for caramel apples.

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:42.420
Fans of RuPaul's Drag Race should have&nbsp;
noticed some familiar faces on screen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:49.080
during Hocus Pocus 2, and honestly, who better&nbsp;
to face off against the three original witches?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:53.340
The Sanderson sisters crash a Halloween&nbsp;
look-alike competition for themselves,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:59.700
coming face to face with Ginger Minj, Kahmora&nbsp;
Hall, and Kornbread. As a notorious drama queen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:02.700
Winnifred is quick to banter&nbsp;
with the other Winnifred.

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:07.440
"Lose the teeth."
"Mind your business girl."

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:13.380
Director Anne Fletcher personally&nbsp;
invited Ginger Minj to join the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:17.460
cast. In an interview with TooFab,&nbsp;
Ginger said that watching the three&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:20.940
witches flying around during&nbsp;
filming caused her to tear up.

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:26.580
"All three of them just take off flying over&nbsp;
our heads and that was the moment where I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:31.380
just had tears streaming down my face...&nbsp;
9-year-old me is living their best life."

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:37.380
Only four of the original Hocus Pocus&nbsp;
actors returned for the second film:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:43.680
Sarah Jessica Parker, Kathy Najimy, Bette&nbsp;
Midler, and the great Doug Jones. That's right,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:48.660
Billy Butcherson, the gentle zombie&nbsp;
and ex-lover, is back for Hocus Pocus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:53.520
2. In the film's opening scenes, Winnifred is&nbsp;
told she'll be marrying John Pritchett. It's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:58.560
then that young Winnifred informs the whole&nbsp;
town that Billy Butcherson is her soulmate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:02.460
especially since they shared that&nbsp;
kiss in the graveyard. Scandalous.

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:08.040
And now, Billy Butcherson is resurrected once&nbsp;
again in service to the Sanderson sisters.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:14.580
However, this time, Billy wants the world to know&nbsp;
that it was "only one kiss," not a fully committed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:19.800
relationship — a running gag that lasts throughout&nbsp;
the film. But the real detail is in how the actor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:26.400
managed to look exactly the same almost 30 years&nbsp;
later. Not only did the costume department create&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:31.980
an identical prosthetic for his face, but they&nbsp;
used the actual wig from the original film.

00:05:31.980 --> 00:05:36.120
"The wig had been sitting on&nbsp;
display at someone's creature shop,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:37.680
and they just took it off and put it back on me."

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:42.600
The original Hocus Pocus is filled&nbsp;
with comedic asides, most of which have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:47.340
helped to make the enduring film a cult&nbsp;
classic. Hocus Pocus 2 is no different,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.340 --> 00:05:52.140
and in fact calls back some of the jokes&nbsp;
and lines from the first film. The most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.140 --> 00:05:56.400
prominent example comes about two-thirds&nbsp;
of the way through the film. On seeing his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.400 --> 00:06:02.100
not-so-beloved Winnifred again, Billy calls&nbsp;
her a withering hag. Fans of the first film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.100 --> 00:06:07.200
should recognize this insult as Thackery Binx&nbsp;
makes his last stand in front of the sisters.

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:11.220
"You hag. There are not enough children in&nbsp;
the world to make you young and beautiful."&nbsp;

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:14.580
"Hag."
"Uh oh."

00:06:14.580 --> 00:06:18.240
So, they promptly turn him into a cat, as you do.

00:06:18.240 --> 00:06:23.280
However, like many misunderstood women,&nbsp;
Winnifred is happy to reclaim the insult&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:26.820
when the sisters search the high&nbsp;
school for Max, Dani, and Allison.

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:34.140
The original Hocus Pocus makes it clear that&nbsp;
the Sanderson sisters are servants of Satan.

00:06:37.451 --> 00:06:38.949
"Master!"

00:06:40.990 --> 00:06:46.080
Allison even tells Max and Dani that their&nbsp;
beloved book was given to them by the devil&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:50.280
himself. However, Hocus Pocus 2 did a&nbsp;
bit of retconning with the introduction&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:55.320
of an evil female mentor dubbed Mother&nbsp;
Witch who gives them the book instead.

00:06:55.320 --> 00:06:58.500
"Magic has a way of uniting&nbsp;
things that ought to be together."

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:04.500
But despite the switcheroo, die-hard audiences&nbsp;
of the original Hocus Pocus will know that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:09.660
mother isn't some random character thoughtlessly&nbsp;
added into the new film. The Sanderson sisters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.660 --> 00:07:15.480
mention their "mother" several times in the&nbsp;
1993 movie, once in a calming circle reminiscing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.480 --> 00:07:21.420
about "mother's scorpion pie" and later when they&nbsp;
salute their long-lost mother with their brooms.

00:07:22.680 --> 00:07:26.760
Only the most eagle-eyed viewers would have&nbsp;
caught the name of the high school displayed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.760 --> 00:07:31.920
in the background behind Becca. In this scene&nbsp;
Becca and Izzy discuss their Halloween plans and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.920 --> 00:07:36.480
right behind them is "Samuel Skelton High&nbsp;
School," written right over the archway.

00:07:36.480 --> 00:07:41.820
While it's tempting to connect the school's name&nbsp;
to the LVCRFT song "Skeleton Sam" that plays at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.820 --> 00:07:46.140
the beginning of the film, Samuel Skelton is&nbsp;
actually a real person from Salem's history.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.140 --> 00:07:52.680
Skelton was the first pastor of the First&nbsp;
Church in Salem, founded on August 6, 1629.

00:07:53.460 --> 00:07:59.040
In modern-day Salem, the Sanderson sisters' spooky&nbsp;
old house has been turned into a delightful magic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:04.020
shop. Naturally, this being a Disney film,&nbsp;
viewers should pay close attention to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:08.940
decorations shown in the background. For instance,&nbsp;
fans of Disney's classic Haunted Mansion ride&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.940 --> 00:08:14.700
should recognize the skull of the "hatbox ghost"&nbsp;
standing out from a group of skulls in one corner.

00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:19.800
That's not all though; sharp-eyed viewers&nbsp;
might have seen the words "Salem Apothecary"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.800 --> 00:08:24.300
written on the corner above the counter,&nbsp;
a clever Easter egg since the Sanderson&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.300 --> 00:08:28.920
sisters talk about their father's apothecary&nbsp;
several times during the film. Finally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:34.500
in one scene, you can spot a basket of plush,&nbsp;
yarn-haired Sanderson sister dolls on a table.

00:08:35.400 --> 00:08:41.400
No one would argue that Book had an important&nbsp;
role in the first Hocus Pocus. The spellbook,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.400 --> 00:08:45.000
which was apparently "bound in human skin," became&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:49.080
an iconic part of the Hocus Pocus&nbsp;
mythology and aesthetic. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.080 --> 00:08:55.440
it's in Hocus Pocus 2 that Book finally gets a&nbsp;
chance to shine, showing off its personality,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.440 --> 00:09:01.560
demonstrating its opinions, and even making&nbsp;
choices about who's going to be its next witch.

00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:06.420
Fans may have noticed that when Book is hiding&nbsp;
from Becca, amongst the other non-sentient&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.420 --> 00:09:13.560
spellbooks, it physically sweats. Because, get&nbsp;
it? It's bound in human skin. As a side note,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.560 --> 00:09:18.120
there's also a reference to Star Trek when&nbsp;
Book refuses to open onto the correct page&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:23.640
for the "Magici Maxima" spell. In a rage,&nbsp;
Winnifred shouts a famous Star Trek line:

00:09:26.239 --> 00:09:27.979
"Resistance is futile!"

00:09:28.345 --> 00:09:33.420
Did that line make it in because Doug Jones,&nbsp;
the actor and contortionist who plays Billy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.420 --> 00:09:39.060
Butcherson, stars as Saru in Star Trek:&nbsp;
Discovery? Or was it just a fun thing to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.060 --> 00:09:42.180
shout out at a book that suddenly&nbsp;
decided to have a mind of its own?

00:09:43.320 --> 00:09:49.500
Movie-goers should know this one already —&nbsp;
stay until after the credits. Hocus Pocus 2&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:53.280
is no different from any other&nbsp;
superhero film, Muppet movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:57.720
or animated film in modern history –&nbsp;
there's always something to see after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.720 --> 00:10:01.920
the credits roll. The original Hocus&nbsp;
Pocus shows Max and Dani's parents,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.920 --> 00:10:06.960
Jenny and Dave, emerging from the town hall a&nbsp;
little worse for wear after their night dancing.

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:12.120
In Hocus Pocus 2 fans are treated to the&nbsp;
possibility of yet another film. Cobweb,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.120 --> 00:10:15.780
Gilbert's black cat, jumps onto&nbsp;
a shelf in the back storeroom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.780 --> 00:10:22.320
nosing among the boxes. Naturally, audiences&nbsp;
can see that one of the boxes is labeled "BF&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.320 --> 00:10:28.980
#2 Candle." Could it be that audiences are&nbsp;
getting a third Hocus Pocus? Let's hope so!

